# 5. PACKAGE CUSTOMIZATION SYSTEM

Build a real, interactive package customization feature for packages where the owner has enabled customization.

Not every package must be customizable.

## Customer experience

When the customer opens a customizable package, show the standard package details and any configured base price.

Below the inclusions, provide an optional “Customize Package” button.

The customer should be able to add from the beginning only those extras that the owner has configured as available add-ons.

Do not allow customers to modify the base package itself, invent new items, alter prices, or remove mandatory inclusions.

Each add-on should display:

- Item name.
- Brief description, where useful.
- Price.
- A clear selection control.

When an add-on is selected or deselected, update the customization summary immediately.

Display:

- Base package price, if configured.
- Each selected add-on.
- Individual add-on prices.
- Subtotal of selected add-ons.
- Final estimated total, where all necessary prices are available.

Use accurate INR formatting.

Calculate totals using numeric values stored in the backend, not by parsing formatted price strings.

Use integer paise for INR monetary calculations where appropriate, to avoid floating-point rounding errors.

If the base package or a selected add-on does not have a configured price, do not invent one or show a misleading total. Instead, clearly state that the final quotation must be confirmed by the owner.

Provide buttons such as:

- “Contact Owner for Quotation”
- “Discuss This Package on WhatsApp”

The final action must open WhatsApp with a prefilled message containing the package name, displayed base price when available, selected add-ons, their prices, and calculated total when valid.

The customer must still manually send the message.

Clearly label the total as an estimate where final pricing depends on availability, location, or other requirements.

Do not treat customization as a confirmed order or booking.

## Admin customization controls

For every package, the owner should be able to:

- Enable or disable customization.
- Set a base price or leave it unlisted.
- Add optional extras.
- Edit extra names, descriptions, and prices.
- Hide or remove an extra.
- Mark inclusions as mandatory.
- Reorder extras.
- Control whether a package is published.

If customization is disabled for a package, hide the customization interface on the public site.

All pricing and package information must come from trusted backend data once connected.

