# 19. FINAL QUALITY STANDARD

The finished website should feel like Movement Craft's own professional digital presence.

It should not look like an untouched AI template. Avoid repetitive generic text, unnecessary gradient blobs, fake statistics, fake reviews, fake portfolio projects, invented discounts, meaningless animations, and decorative controls that do nothing.

Focus on authentic branding, thoughtful composition, elegant black-and-gold styling, excellent mobile usability, and clear customer journeys.

The website is an enquiry and service-discovery platform. It is not an automated booking engine, payment portal, or customer account system.

The owner must have control over the published website through the private admin panel.

**Most important acceptance criterion:** Once the backend is connected and the website is deployed, the owner should be able to log into the admin panel, edit a service or package, save the change, and see that change reflected on the public website without editing code or redeploying the application.

Build the application to this standard. If a requirement cannot be completed with the current environment or available free-tier services, explain the exact limitation and implement the closest secure, functional alternative rather than silently substituting a mockup.

